Z||000000||fierohuddy||09-23-2001||03:51 PM||||What's the best and safest method for cleaning the engine?<P>Thanks,<P>Simon||||reg||5
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||09-23-2001||05:19 PM||||Welcome to the spot Simon!!!!!<BR>You will find many different answers to this?<BR>It has been talked about over and over again<P>This is just to help you use the form to it's best!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> There is a search mode (top right of this page) click on it, type in the search word.....Engine cleaning, engine compartment, any word for what your looking for. It's easy to use and you'll get more info than you need. Hope this helps.<P><BR>DXR_DAD<P>||||reg||14
Z||000002||fierohuddy||09-23-2001||05:24 PM||||I did actually do the search and there were various threads, but all seemed to relate to power washing.  One mentioned using engine cleaner but said nothing about results.  I guess the specific question is, can I just spray some engine cleaner on it,  wait, rinse it off, and then polish the whole thing with a rag and some basic cleaner solution?<P>Thanks,<P>Simon<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DXR_DAD:<BR><B>Welcome to the spot Simon!!!!!<BR>You will find many different answers to this?<BR>It has been talked about over and over again<P>This is just to help you use the form to it's best!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> There is a search mode (top right of this page) click on it, type in the search word.....Engine cleaning, engine compartment, any word for what your looking for. It's easy to use and you'll get more info than you need. Hope this helps.<P><BR>DXR_DAD<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||09-23-2001||05:31 PM||||Yep, that sounds the best if it's not real grimmie!!!! engine cleaner, gojo hand soap,<BR>mild soap, any of these, try to cover all sensors, dist, & elect. connections I use safeway plastic bags? and don't spray water directly on them.<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||09-23-2001||08:33 PM||||I usually empty half a pump-bottle of de-greaser, (WHILE THE ENGINE IS RUNNING!!!!!!!) then hose it down with m'garden hose. Bear in mind, though, that I've packed almost all of my electrical connections with lithium grease to stop shorting. After that, I just spray in some WD-40 on the exposed bits. Makes it look shiny for about 3 days, before the dust from my road turns my engine yellow  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><BR>Better results, but more expensive is "tire wax" on all your fittings. I still prefer WD-40 though, even though it smells funny for the first 15 minutes of running  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Just be careful not to set your headers on fire  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000005||ka4nkf||09-25-2001||12:01 AM||||I use automotive simple green. Spray the engine while it is cold then spray simple green everywhere. let set for thirty minutes then hose off. does a good job if your motor is not real greasy. get at auto zone for $7.99 gal.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ambush||09-25-2001||10:45 AM||||its simple. ENGINE DEGREASER everywhere (except electronics) let it sit for about 5 minutes then use a pressure washer at a light setting and go in from the top. After that's done more degreaser onthe undercarriage then pressure wash on high from the bottom Note:AVOID THE CAP and ROTOR||||reg||1
